# The annotations of the game image: the single source of truth for src/game/*.asm (kit/mkgame.py).
# The format is in kit/mkgame.py, class Annotations. One line an entry:
#
#   @module NAME ; title            the entries from here on go to NAME.asm, the title heads the file
#   @about a paragraph              the module file's header text, one paragraph a line
#   $ADDR c Name ; title            a routine
#   > a description line
#   $ADDR b Name ; title            data (w words, t text, s space; "b Name 8" rows of 8)
#   @res graphics/NAME.bin          the entry is a resource: src/res/..., INCBIN
#   $ADDR Name ; comment            a label and comment inside an entry: on an instruction, or on the data line
#                                   that starts at ADDR (a data entry's rows are cut there)
#   @isub $ADDR LD HL,-6            the instruction written so
#   @equ $ADDR Name [N] ; comment    a variable past the image: an EQU, its operands by name
#   @inline $ADDR                   a routine that reads its data after the CALL
#   @names BANK PATH, @bank $ADDR BANK   an address in RAM bank BANK, named by the .ann of that bank
#
# Terramex (Grandslam 1987): TZX block 5, $7200-$FFFF, the game proper. The other parts of the tape have their own
# .ann files: src/tape/basic.ann (the BASIC loader), src/screen/screen.ann, src/music/music.ann (the AY player, RAM 6),
# src/select/select.ann (the 128K set-up and the explorer selector, RAM 1) and src/explorers/explorers.ann.
#
# Credit: the SkoolKit disassembly of Terramex by Nikita Zimin (nzeemin, github.com/nzeemin/skoolkit-game-revs,
# terramex-zx, commit 6a328b3b) was the starting point for the names, the routine boundaries and the data shapes. A
# title taken from it says "(SK)"; every name and description here was checked against the code and the recordings,
# and work/stage2/NOTES.md lists each name, boundary and meaning changed from it and why.

@names 1 ../select/select.ann ; RAM 1 at $C000: the explorer selector (src/select)
@names 6 ../music/music.ann ; RAM 6 at $C000: the AY music player (src/music)
@bank $C000 1
@bank $C000 6
@isub $8F5B LD BC,SelectorStart
@isub $8F5E CALL SelectorStart
@isub $94A0 CALL MusicFrame

@equ $4000 Screen 6144 ; the screen's pixels
@equ $5800 Attributes 768 ; the screen's attributes
@equ $5B03 InfiniteLives 1 ; 1 when $8000 held $C9 before the load (the loader); GameEntry then makes $A9FD OR A
@equ $5B04 Hero 4 ; object slot 0, the hero: X, Y, frame ($7F hidden), flags (bit 7 facing)
@equ $5B08 ObjectSlot1 4 ; object slots 1-3: the room's creatures; the room scripts borrow 2-4
@equ $5B0C ObjectSlot2 4
@equ $5B10 ObjectSlot3 4
@equ $5B14 ObjectSlot4 4
@equ $5B24 PrevActorRects 32 ; last pass's ActorRects (RenderPass copies 32 bytes)
@equ $5B44 ActorRects 20 ; per slot: back-buffer address, row plotter
@equ $5B70 Explorer 1 ; the chosen explorer 0-4, $FF before the first choice
@equ $5B72 TilePixelsPtr 2 ; the tile pixels' base, TilePixels $F000
@equ $5B78 HiScore 4 ; 32 bits, low byte first
@equ $5B7C BearerLoads 27 ; the item each of the 27 invisible bearers carries, $FF none
@equ $5B97 Lives 1 ; 4 at the start
@equ $5B98 HeldItem 1 ; the item in hand, $FF none
@equ $5B99 Thought 3 ; the thought bubble's X, Y and item ($FE: gone)
@equ $5B9E LiftRoom 1 ; the room the lift is in
@equ $5B9F LiftY 1 ; the lift platform's Y + 8
@equ $5BA0 NotOnLift 1 ; 1 each pass, 0 while the hero stands on the lift
@equ $5BA1 ProfessorState 1 ; the professor's script state in room $3B
@equ $5BA2 WellHole 2 ; the tile-map address of the well's hole, 0 none
@equ $5BA4 WellTiles 2 ; the well back-tile's rows 1-2 in BackTiles
@equ $5BA6 DigitBuffer 3 ; PrintByte's three digits
@equ $5BD6 PanelColumns 24 ; up to 12 column pointers for BlitColumns
@equ $5BFA UnicycleFrames 1 ; $3C while riding the unicycle in room $2F
@equ $5BFB CountdownDays 1 ; the countdown: 30 days 23:59 at the start
@equ $5BFC CountdownHours 1
@equ $5BFD CountdownMinutes 1
@equ $5BFE GameWon 1 ; $1D after the professor's sixth gift: the asteroid is deflected
@equ $5BFF GameOver 1
@equ $5C00 BallThrown 1 ; room $2D's cricket ball thrown
@equ $5C01 Room 1 ; level x 12 + column, $14 at the start
@equ $5C02 PassCount 1 ; +1 every main-loop pass
@equ $5C03 RefuseCount 1 ; refusals of a big drop in a row
@equ $5C04 Falling 1 ; 1 while falling
@equ $5C05 FallPasses 1 ; passes of the fall, 20 or more kill on landing
@equ $5C06 Status 1 ; the hero's status 0-33 (StatusHandlers)
@equ $5C07 StatusTimer 1 ; cleared by SetStatus, counted by the handlers
@equ $5C08 JumpDirection 1 ; the input bits a jump moves by
@equ $5C09 HeroSavedXY 2 ; X, Y at the start of the pass
@equ $5C0C BridgeState 1 ; the expanding bridge of rooms $19 and $3A
@equ $5C0D BridgeReverse 1
@equ $5C0E ItemSlot1 5 ; the room's floor items: X, Y, item ($FF none, $FE taken), the ItemPlaces record
@equ $5C13 ItemSlot2 5
@equ $5C18 Score 4 ; 32-bit signed
@equ $5C1C NumberWork 4 ; PrintNumber's copy
@equ $5C20 DigitShown 1 ; PrintNumber: a digit printed
@equ $5C21 BearerScrollDir 1 ; 1 key 1 (right), 0 key 2
@equ $5C22 BearerPhase 1 ; the bearer row's 4-step scroll
@equ $5C23 BearerIndex 1 ; the first bearer shown, 0-$1A
@equ $5C24 RopeCount 1 ; the rope of room $10 ($0D whole), drawn in room $1C
@equ $5C25 BalloonX 1 ; the balloon of rooms 3 and $0F: X, Y, room
@equ $5C26 BalloonY 1
@equ $5C27 BalloonInRoom 1
@equ $5C28 MudTile 1 ; $BC / $BD under the feet, else 0
@equ $5C29 MudPasses 1 ; passes on mud, 50 sinks
@equ $5C2A LifeLost 1 ; $32 when the death wait ends: MainLoop respawns
@equ $5C2B RespawnStatus 1 ; the respawn point: Status, StatusTimer, Room, the hero's X, Y, frame, flags, LiftRoom, LiftY
@equ $5C2C RespawnTimer 1
@equ $5C2D RespawnRoom 1
@equ $5C2E RespawnXY 2
@equ $5C30 RespawnFrame 2
@equ $5C32 RespawnLift 2
@equ $5C34 FloatVelocity 2 ; room $2C: C = X, B = Y velocity
@equ $5C3C WantedItem 1 ; the item the professor asks for
@equ $5C3D GiftCount 1 ; the gifts given, 0-6
@equ $5C3E LastGift 1
@equ $5C3F PillsTaken 1 ; the Anti Radiation Pills picked up
@equ $5C40 RoomFlag 1 ; per room: the basket's end ($3F), the lever latch ($3E, $40)
@equ $5C41 RoomStage 1 ; the room script's stage, cleared on room entry
@equ $5C42 LeverState 1
@equ $5C43 SwitchFitted 1
@equ $5C44 CrystalPlaced 1 ; the Energy Crystal placed in room $30: the teleport pads work
@equ $5C45 CrossState 1 ; the Silver Cross creature: 0 waiting, 1 fleeing, $FF gone
@equ $5C46 BlankIcon 72 ; 72 zero bytes, the empty panel icon
@equ $5E00 StackTop 1
@equ $5F5F Im2Jump 3 ; JP Im2Handler, written by GameEntry
@equ $5FE5 Last7FFD 1 ; the last value sent to port $7FFD
@equ $5FE6 PagingStub 3 ; the selector's paging stub (OUT (C),A; RET once patched)
@equ $5FFE Has128K 1 ; $11 on a 128K, 0 on a 48K
@equ $5FFF GameLoaded 1 ; 1 from GameEntry: the selector returns to the game
@equ $6000 ExplorerSet 4608 ; the chosen explorer's sprites: frames $00-$3F of the sprite space

@isub $8F44 LD (LifeLossOp),A
@isub $8FCF LD HL,$6070
@isub $91F7 LD DE,$6000
@isub $93A2 LD DE,$8F47
@isub $91E6 LD DE,TilePixels+$B5*8
@isub $9299 LD DE,TilePixels+$8C*8
@isub $985D LD HL,$FF02
@isub $99F4 LD DE,$6020
@isub $9A56 LD BC,$6000
@isub $9B99 LD HL,$7E6F
@isub $9E5D LD HL,ExplorerSet+9*72
@isub $A102 LD IY,HeroProbes
@isub $A3E4 LD IY,HeroProbes
@isub $A2A6 LD DE,TileMap


@module sprites ; The sprite space past the explorer set: the creatures and the items
$7200 b CreatureSprites 8 ; The creatures' sprites: frames $40-$7E of the sprite space, 63 sprites of 24 x 24
> The sprite space starts at ExplorerSet $6000: frame F lies at $6000 + 72 x F, frames $00-$3F the chosen explorer's set, $40-$7E these, $7F the blank frame BlankSprite $83B8, $80 + n item n (ItemSprites $8400). Each sprite is three columns of 24 bytes, left column first, top byte first, ink 1. The plotter $9C7E reads them through the frame number ($9FAA computes the address); RenderPass $9B22 draws them with a one-pixel outline from OutlineMasks $FF00, mirrored through BitReverse $FE00 when flags bit 7 is set (the stored graphics face left, so bit 7 set faces right).
> The frames: the professor and his poses, the snake, the crocodile, the bird, the frog, the stone faces, the treasure chest, the drops, the comet, the planets of the space scene (src/res/sprites/creatures.png).
> Witness: every play build reads $7200-$7D40, $7E18-$82E0; the frames at $7D41-$7E17 and $82E1-$83B7 are read in no play build (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx x31 byte counts; work/stage2/bytemap.py).
@res sprites/creatures.bin
$83B8 b BlankSprite 8 ; Frame $7F: 72 zero bytes, the empty sprite
> Read in every play build (bytemap.py): a slot with nothing to show draws this frame.
$8400 b ItemSprites 8 ; The 32 items' sprites, frames $80-$9F of the sprite space
> 72 bytes each in the creatures' layout. DrawItem $9DE3 draws item n from $8400 + 72 x n. The names are in src/res/sprites/README.md (SK's names, checked against the pictures).
> Witness: every byte read in play except $8BE1-$8C27, item $1C (Barrel Small) after its first byte: the item is never shown in the recordings.
@res sprites/items.bin

@module entry ; GameEntry, the IM 2 table and the game's start
$8D00 b Var8D00 ; A game variable inside the image, set to 0 by GameEntry $8F00
$8D01 b Leftover8D01 ; Leftover: 255 bytes no code reads (350 of the 511 bytes up to $8EFF are zeros)
> No play build reads or writes $8D01-$8DFF (bytemap.py).
@res leftovers/8d01.bin
$8E00 b Im2Table 16 ; The IM 2 table: on the tape, leftover bytes; GameEntry fills $8E00-$8F00 with $5F
> GameEntry $8F00 writes 257 bytes of $5F from $8E00, its own first byte $8F00 included (the SkoolKit snapshot, taken after it, holds $5F there). With I = $8E and the bus at $FF the CPU reads the vector from $8EFF and $8F00: $5F5F, where GameEntry put JP $9491. Witness: the play L1 counts 69582 reads of $8EFF (and of $8F00) against 78587 interrupts in the same builds, so the count is a lower bound, not one read an interrupt; no other byte of the table is read.
@res leftovers/im2-table-tape.bin
$8F00 c GameEntry ; Game entry: the IM 2 table and vector, the stack, the 128K page, the life-loss patch
> The last tape block's loader jumps here (`JP $8F00` of the BASIC loader's code, c1 frame 21597). With interrupts off it writes `$10` to Last7FFD `$5FE5` (RAM 0 at `$C000`, ROM 1: the value the IM 2 handler `$9491` pages back after the music), fills the IM 2 table `$8E00-$8F00` (257 bytes) with `$5F`, puts `JP $9491` at `$5F5F` (the vector every interrupt reaches with I = `$8E`), sets SP to `$5E00`, I to `$8E`, IM 2 and EI.
> Then: `$5FFF` = 1 (the selector, run again from NewGame `$8F47`, reads it: the game has been loaded), border 0, `$8D00` = 0, the high score `$5B78-$5B7B` = 0 (it is cleared only here, so it survives from game to game), and the life-loss patch: the opcode at `$A9FD` (the `DEC (HL)` on Lives in `$A9EE`) is written `$35` (`DEC (HL)`) or, when `$5B03` is not 0, `$B7` (`OR A`): lives are never lost. The BASIC loader sets `$5B03` to 1 when `$8000` held `$C9` before the load (doc 3, 3.2): a cheat hook for a front end that pokes `$8000`. In c1 `$5B03` is 0 (`$8F41` not executed in any recording).
> Falls into NewGame `$8F47`.
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$8F0C FillIm2Table ; B = 0: 256 bytes of $5F, then the 257th
$8F2E ; the byte at $8D00 = 0 (read by $9C7E in play)
$8F31 ; the high score $5B78-$5B7B = 0
$8F39 ; C = $35, the opcode DEC (HL)
$8F3B ; $5B03 = 1: the loader saw $C9 at $8000
$8F41 ; C = $B7, the opcode OR A: Lives never decreases
$8F43 SetLifeLossOp ; the opcode at $A9FD ($A9EE: DEC (HL) on Lives)
$8F47 c NewGame ; Start a game: the device menu, the explorer selector, the set-up of a new game
> Reached from GameEntry `$8F00` (falls in) and from EndGame `$906D` (`JP $8F47`) after every game: c1 2 runs, explorers 5, gameover 1, rzx50000 1.
> 1. DeviceMenu `$93AF` until 0 is pressed.
> 2. On a 128K (Has128K `$5FFE` not 0): pages RAM 1 in (`$7FFD` = `$11`, kept in Last7FFD `$5FE5`) and calls `$C000` with BC = `$C000`: the explorer selector, which the 128K setup copied to RAM 1 and relocated there; it copies the chosen explorer's data set to `$6000-$71FF` and returns; then RAM 0 is paged back (`$10`). On a 48K the explorer was chosen during the load (the selector runs in place before the last block), so the same explorer plays every game.
> 3. The set-up (InitGame `$8F69`): clears `$5B04-$5B67` (the hero and party records and other state, 100 bytes: one stored, 99 copied by the LDIR at `$8F74`); fills BearerLoads `$5B7C-$5B96` (27 bytes) with `$FF` (free); ResetItems `$B932` clears the taken bits (bit 7) of the 31 ItemPlaces records and bit 7 of `$B9D9` is set again; copies the saved panel back to the screen (`$E000` -> `$5000`, 2048 bytes; `$E800` -> `$5A00`, 256 attributes: EndGame `$906D` saved it there, because play uses `$E000-$EFFF` as the background copy of the play window); the tile bitmap pointer `$5B72` = `$F000`; `$5C3C`, `$A6FD`, `$A700`, `$5B98`, `$5B9B` = `$FF`, `$A6F5` = 7, `$5B06` = 0; clears `$5BFA-$5C8D` (148 bytes: the countdown, GameOver, Room, PassCount, Status and the rest); `$BCF2` with DE = 0; the object at `$5C25-$5C27` = X `$70`, Y `$60`, room `$0F`; Room `$5C01` = `$14` and the room set-up `$9855`; `$9EBD`; Lives `$5B97` = 4 and `$9E96` (the lives in the panel); the hero at X `$0A` (`$5B04`), Y `$60` (`$5B05`); the lift (`$AF81`) in room `$2B` (`$5B9E`) at Y `$30` (`$5B9F`); the countdown 30 days 23:59 (`$5BFB` days = `$1E`, `$5BFC` hours = `$17`, `$5BFD` minutes = `$3B`); `$9AA1` copies the start into the respawn state `$5C2B-$5C33`; `$9E5D`. Falls into MainLoop `$9018`.
> Witness: L1 9 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx).
$8F4A c RunSelector ; The explorer selector on a 128K, then the new game (NewGame continued)
> The return point of NewGame's `CALL $93AF`: an entry of its own only because the explorers recording starts inside DeviceMenu, so its L1 sees the RET land here. Step 2 and 3 of NewGame `$8F47`: on a 128K the selector at `$C000` in RAM 1, then InitGame `$8F69`. Falls into MainLoop `$9018`.
> Witness: L1 8 (c1, explorers, rzx).
$8F50 ; page RAM 1 in: the relocated explorer selector at $C000
$8F5B ; BC = the selector's base, $C000
$8F5E ; the selector: the chosen explorer's set to $6000-$71FF
$8F62 ; RAM 0 back at $C000
$8F69 InitGame ; the new game's variables
$8F76 ; BearerLoads: 27 bytes of $FF (free)
$8F86 ; bit 7 of $B9D9 set again
$8F8B ; the panel saved by EndGame back on the screen: $E000 -> $5000 (2048), $E800 -> $5A00 (256)
$8F9E ; the tile bitmaps are at $F000
$8FBE ; clear $5BFA-$5C8D (148 bytes): Countdown, GameOver, Room, PassCount, Status, ...
$8FCF ; X $70, Y $60 to $5C25/$5C26: a constant, not an address
$8FE0 ; the first room: $14
$8FEB ; Lives = 4
$8FF3 ; the hero's Y = $60
$8FF8 ; the hero's X = $0A
$8FFD ; the lift's room = $2B
$9002 ; the lift's Y = $30
$9007 ; the countdown: 30 days ($5BFB), 23 hours ($5BFC), 59 minutes ($5BFD)
$9012 ; the start is the first respawn state ($5C2B-$5C33)

@module mainloop ; The main loop, the end of a game and the restart after a lost life
$9018 c MainLoop ; The main loop: one pass of the game, no frame sync
> One pass: `$5BA0` = 1 (`$AF81` clears it on the lift); IX = the hero record `$5B04`; when Room `$5C01` equals the lift's room `$5B9E`, `$AF81` (the lift); `$A3E1` (the hero: input, movement, the Status handlers); when LifeLost `$5C2A` is set, Respawn `$9090`; else `$B9FA` (the items), RoomEffects `$91C0`, CountDown `$935D` (one minute a pass), `$BE98` (the creatures), `$9B22` (the sprites; it calls ShowCapsules `$92BD`); GameOver `$5BFF` set ends the game (EndGame `$906D`); PassCount `$5C02` + 1.
> The keys at the end of a pass: Q held with CAPS SHIFT ends the game (the abort: c1 and explorers, 6 runs of `$9059`); Q held with A held freezes the game until A is let go (`$9062`, not executed in any recording); Q alone does nothing.
> There is no HALT: a pass takes as long as its work. In the rzx segments the day rolls over (`$936B`, 13 runs, one in every segment of about 4000 frames) every 1440 passes, so a pass is about 2.8 frames (WALKTHROUGH 1: 2.4 to 3.3).
> Witness: L1 26517 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$9018 ; $5BA0 = 1 every pass ($AF81 clears it)
$9021 ; in the lift's room ($5B9E)? the lift $AF81
$902B ; the hero: input, movement, Status
$902E ; a life lost ($5C2A set by $A9EE)? respawn
$9037 ; the flames, beams and capsules
$903A ; one minute off the countdown every pass
$9043 ; GameOver set (the space scene ended, or the ending)?
$9049 ; PassCount + 1
$9050 ; Q held?
$9059 ; and CAPS SHIFT: abort
$9062 FreezeWhileA ; Q without CAPS SHIFT: wait while A is held
$906D c EndGame ; End a game: the high score, the panel saved, the base tile set back, the menu
> Reached from MainLoop `$9018` when GameOver `$5BFF` is set (gameover frame 1962 after the space scene; rzx50000 frame 732 after the ending) or on CAPS SHIFT + Q (c1, explorers).
> `$BD50` keeps the score as the high score when it is higher; then the panel (the screen's bottom third `$5000-$57FF` and its attributes `$5A00-$5AFF`) is saved to `$E000-$E7FF` and `$E800-$E8FF`, where DeviceMenu `$93AF` takes its frame pieces from and InitGame `$8F69` restores it; when the alternate tile set is in (AltTileset `$918C` not 0), SwapTileset `$918D` puts the base set back (not executed in any recording: every game ended in a base-set room); `JP $8F47`.
> Witness: L1 8 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx).
$9070 ; the panel's bitmap to $E000
$907B ; its attributes to $E800
$9086 ; the base tile set back for the next game
$9090 c Respawn ; Restart after a lost life from the respawn state
> Reached from MainLoop `$9018` when LifeLost `$5C2A` is set (`$A9EE` sets it to `$32` when StatusTimer `$5C07` reaches 50 and takes a life). gameover frame 1509 (the last life; `$A9EE` went on to LoseGame `$9372`, which put room `$28` and Status `$1D` in the respawn state, so this respawn starts the space scene), rzx 4 runs.
> Clears LifeLost and `$5C05`; copies the respawn state back: Status `$5C06` from `$5C2B`, StatusTimer `$5C07` from `$5C2C`, the hero record `$5B04-$5B07` from `$5C2E-$5C31`, Room `$5C01` from `$5C2D`, the lift `$5B9E-$5B9F` from `$5C32-$5C33` (`$9AA1` writes the state on every room entry); the room set-up `$9855`; `$5B9B` = `$FE`; back to MainLoop.
> Witness: L1 5 (gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).

@module util ; Printing, distances, random numbers
$90C6 c PrintChar ; Print a character of the ROM font at a screen address
> A = the character code, HL = the screen address (top pixel row of a cell). Copies the 8 bytes of the ROM font (`$3C00` + 8A: `$3D00` is the space) down the cell (INC D). Out: HL + 1 (the next column); BC, DE kept.
> Callers: PrintString `$94F9` (the menu), `$BD75`/`$BD78` (the score and high score), PrintDigitAt `$9136`.
> Witness: L1 1933 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$90D0 ; the ROM font: $3C00 + 8 * code
$90D6 PrintCharRow
$90E1 c PrintByte ; Print A in decimal, left-aligned in three columns
> A = 0-255, DE = the screen address. Builds three ASCII digits at `$5BA6-$5BA8` (hundreds, tens, units, by repeated subtraction), skips the leading zeros (the units digit always prints), prints the digits through PrintDigitAt `$9136` and then a space for each skipped zero, so the field is always three cells.
> The only callers are at `$A7F4`, `$A7FD` and `$A806` (the countdown's days, hours and minutes after a text printed by PrintString `$94F9`): not executed in any recording (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx x31); known only from the code.
> Witness: L1 0 ().
$90E7 PrintByteHundreds
$90F0 PrintByteTensStart
$90F3 PrintByteTens
$90FC PrintByteUnitsStart
$90FF PrintByteUnits
$9107 PrintByteDigits ; B = 1 + the leading zeros
$911A PrintByte3Digits
$911F PrintByte2Digits
$9124 PrintByte1Digit
$912D PrintBytePad ; a space for each leading zero
$9134 PrintByteDone
$9136 c PrintDigitAt ; Print the character at (HL) at screen DE
> HL = the character, DE = the screen address; PrintChar `$90C6`; HL and DE kept. Called three times by PrintByte `$90E1`; not executed in any recording; known only from the code.
> Witness: L1 0 ().
$9140 c Near ; Are two objects within 16 (or 8) pixels on both axes?
> IX = the first object (X at +0, Y at +1, the sprite frame at +2), IY = the second (X, Y). The distance is 16, or 8 when IX's frame is `$5C-$5F` (`$914E`: rzx only, 3169 runs). Out: carry set when |X1 - X2| and |Y1 - Y2| are both below it. BC kept.
> Callers: `$B44A`, `$B5E1`, `$B74D`/`$B765`, `$BB70` (52660 calls), `$C0E0`: the touch test of the hero against items and creatures. The SkoolKit title ("classify object type") names only its first lines.
> Witness: L1 67291 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$9150 NearDx
$915A NearCheckX
$9167 NearCheckY
$9168 NearDone ; carry: within the distance

@module ending ; The game over, the space scene and the ending
$916A c InvertPlayWindow ; Swap ink and paper in the play window's attributes
> XORs every attribute of `$5800-$59FF` (character rows 0-15, the play window) with `$3F`: ink 7-ink, paper 7-paper, BRIGHT and FLASH kept. Called twice it restores the screen.
> The only callers are `JP $916A` at `$B1E8` and `CALL $916A` at `$B1EE`, in the ending's code after `$B0B6`: not executed in any recording (rzx50000 runs the ending from `$B0B6` to `$B169`); known only from the code.
> Witness: L1 0 ().
$9171 InvertPlayWindowLoop

@module rooms ; The room set-up, the tile sets, the tile map and the room effects
$917C c ClearPartySlots ; Party slots 1-4: frame $7F, flags 0
> Writes `$007F` to the words `$5B0A`, `$5B0E`, `$5B12`, `$5B16`: bytes +2 (the sprite frame) and +3 of the four 4-byte records after the hero's (`$5B04`). Frame `$7F` is the blank sprite: `$6000 + $7F * 72` = `$83B8`, 72 zero bytes in the image. Called by the room set-up at `$990B` on every room entry (106 runs over all builds).
> Witness: L1 106 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$918C b AltTileset ; The tile set in place: 0 the base set, $FF the alternate set
> Toggled only by SwapTileset `$918D`; read by the room set-up `$9880` (which swaps the set for the 15 rooms of the list at `$9AC6`), RoomEffects `$91C0`, ShowCapsules `$92BD`, EndGame `$906D`, `$A102`, `$A193` and others. Written in rzx18000, rzx20000, rzx26000 (twice), rzx34000, rzx50000.
$918D c SwapTileset ; Exchange the base and the alternate tile set
> Swaps the 1024 bytes of `$F400-$F7FF` (the bitmaps of tiles `$80-$FF`) with `$FA00-$FDFF`, and the 128 attributes of those tiles `$DF80-$DFFF` with `$C580-$C5FF`; then AltTileset `$918C` = NOT its old value. A swap, not a copy: the set that goes out is kept for the way back.
> Callers: the room set-up at `$9890`/`$9899` (6 runs: rzx18000 frame 1417, rzx20000 858, rzx26000 463 and 1075, rzx34000 1481, rzx50000 183), EndGame at `$908A`.
> Witness: L1 6 (rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$919A SwapTileBitmaps
$91A8 ; the attributes of tiles $80-$FF: $C580 <-> $DF80
$91B0 SwapTileAttrs
$91C0 c RoomEffects ; Animate the flames (base set), the beams and the capsules (alternate set)
> Called once a pass by MainLoop `$9018`. The lists are built by the room set-up `$9880` with `$9A8C` (a CPIR over the tile map `$F800`): `$9AD5` holds the map addresses of tile `$B5` in a base-set room, of tile `$DD` in an alternate-set room; `$9AE5` those of tile `$8C` (alternate set only); a 0 word ends a list.
> Base set (AltTileset `$918C` = 0): for the first two entries of `$9AD5` (B = 2) the 8-byte frame PassCount AND 3 of FlameFrames `$933D` is copied into tile `$B5`'s bitmap (`$F5A8`), the cell is drawn again on the screen and in the background copy (`$9A52`), and its attribute (map address + `$6000` = `$5800 + offset`) gets BRIGHT flipped at random (bit 0 of R). The rooms with tile `$B5` (from the room data): `$1C`, `$21`, `$29`, `$2D`, `$2E`, `$2F`, `$33`, `$35`, `$36`, `$3F`, `$40`, `$41`, `$42`. gameover (room `$1C`) and 11 rzx segments run it (5256 runs of `$91D6`).
> Alternate set (Beams `$9208`): `$9AD5` is read as pairs of tile `$DD` cells on one row: the two ends of an electric beam. Pixel rows 6 and 7 of each cell between them get random bytes (R rotated, XOR PassCount); the beam is redrawn every pass (rzx26000-rzx42000, 9538 runs of `$9266`). The hero is hit when his X is from the left end's X to below the right end's X minus 12 and |Y + 6 - the row's Y| < 12, while Status `$5C06` is below 4: Status = `$18` through `$AE85` (CreatureDeath `$A89E` in the table at `$A72E`). The hit (`$9260`) is not executed in any recording. A list that ends after an odd entry returns without the capsules. Rooms with tile `$DD`: `$20`, `$38` (two beams), `$39`, `$3A`, `$3C`, `$43`. rzx42000 frame 500 shows the beam of room `$3A` across row 13.
> Then the capsules (Capsules `$9282`): the 16-byte frame of CapsuleFrames `$92FD` (PassCount AND 3, run backwards when bit 2 of PassCount is clear: 3 2 1 0 0 1 2 3) is copied into tiles `$8C`-`$8D` (`$F460`), and each cell of `$9AE5` gets tile `$8C` and the next cell `$8D` again in the map and the background copy (`$9A4D`); ShowCapsules `$92BD` copies them to the screen later in the pass. Rooms with tile `$8C`: `$12`, `$20`, `$2B`, `$2C`, `$38`, `$3A`, `$3B` (six: the lab, rzx46000 frame 500), `$3C`, `$44`.
> Witness: L1 26513 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$91C9 ; the alternate set: beams and capsules
$91CC FlamesLoop
$91D7 ; the frame: PassCount AND 3
$91E6 ; into tile $B5's bitmap
$91F1 ; draw tile $B5 there: the screen and the background copy
$91F7 ; the map address + $6000: the cell's attribute
$91FB ; flip BRIGHT at random
$9203 FlamesNext
$9208 Beams ; a beam: the left and the right end cells
$9215 ; the right end; 0: the list ended inside a pair
$921F ; the screen addresses of pixel row 6 of the cells
$9237 ; the ends as pixel coordinates: H = Y, L = X
$9240 ; the hero inside the beam's X span?
$924B ; and within 12 rows of it?
$9255 BeamCheckY
$9259 ; and Status below 4?
$9260 ; the hero is hit: Status $18
$9265 BeamDraw
$9266 BeamLoop ; random bytes on pixel rows 6 and 7 of each cell
$9282 c Capsules ; Animate the capsules, tiles $8C-$8D (RoomEffects continued)
> Reached only by `JP Z,$9282` at `$9212` when Beams `$9208` meets the 0 word that ends the list `$9AD5` (an entry of the cut because it is a jump target from another routine's L1 block). Described under RoomEffects `$91C0`: the frame of CapsuleFrames `$92FD` (3 2 1 0 0 1 2 3 over PassCount) into the bitmaps of tiles `$8C`-`$8D` (`$F460`), then tile `$8C` and `$8D` at each map address of `$9AE5` and the next, in the map and the background copy (`$9A4D`).
> Witness: L1 5581 (rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$9282 ; the frame for the capsules: 3 2 1 0 0 1 2 3
$928E CapsulesFrame
$9299 ; into tiles $8C-$8D's bitmaps
$92A4 CapsulesLoop
$92AE ; tile $8C at the cell, $8D at the next: the map and the background copy
$92BD c ShowCapsules ; Copy the capsule cells from the background copy to the screen
> Called by `$9B22` at `$9BE4` every pass. Returns at once in a base-set room (AltTileset `$918C` = 0). Else, for each map address in the list `$9AE5`, copies the cell and the one to its right from the background copy (`$E000`) to the screen through CopyBackCell `$92D6` (33546 calls, rzx18000-rzx50000).
> Witness: L1 26510 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$92C5 ShowCapsulesLoop
$92D6 c CopyBackCell ; Copy one cell of the play window from the background copy to the screen
> HL = a tile map address (`$F800-$F9FF`). The cell's screen address is (H AND 3) * 8 + `$40` : L, its background copy the same OR `$E0`; 8 bytes down the cell. HL and DE kept. The SkoolKit note ("menu border strip") does not fit: the only caller is ShowCapsules `$92BD`.
> Witness: L1 33546 (rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$92E7 CopyBackCellLoop
$92F0 c MapToPixels ; A tile map address as pixel coordinates
> HL = a tile map address (`$F800` + row * 32 + column). Out: H = row * 8 (the Y), L = column * 8 (the X), the units of the hero's X and Y at `$5B04`/`$5B05`. Called twice by Beams `$9208` (3646 calls). The SkoolKit title ("attribute address") does not fit what it returns.
> Witness: L1 3646 (rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$92FD b CapsuleFrames 8 ; Four frames of the capsule, tiles $8C-$8D: 16 bytes each, the left tile then the right
> Copied to `$F460` by Capsules `$9282`. The frames differ only in rows 3-6 of the right tile. Read in rzx18000-rzx50000.
$930D ; frame 1
$931D ; frame 2
$932D ; frame 3
@res graphics/capsules.bin
$933D b FlameFrames 8 ; Four 8-byte frames of tile $B5, a flame, PassCount AND 3 picks one
> Copied into tile $B5's bitmap ($F5A8) by RoomEffects $91E2 for the first two flames of a base-set room (13 rooms hold tile $B5), then the cell is drawn again. Read in gameover (room $1C) and 11 rzx segments.
$9345 ; frame 1
$934D ; frame 2
$9355 ; frame 3
@res graphics/flames.bin

@module countdown ; The countdown and the lost game
$935D c CountDown ; One minute off the countdown; when it runs out, the game is lost
> Called once a pass by MainLoop `$9018`. The countdown is three plain binary bytes: days `$5BFB`, hours `$5BFC`, minutes `$5BFD` (InitGame sets 30, 23, 59; c1 frame 23500 holds 30, 23, 11). Minutes - 1; below 0 it is 59 and the hours - 1 (440 runs of `$9364`); below 0, 23 and the days - 1 (`$936B`, 13 runs in rzx: about every 4000 frames); below 0 the time is up: falls into LoseGame `$9372` (not executed in any recording: the rzx run ended with 18 days left).
> Witness: L1 26514 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$9372 c LoseGame ; The game is lost: the hero in room $28 for the space scene
> Reached by falling in from CountDown `$935D` (the time is up) and by `JP Z,$9372` at `$A9FE` in `$A9EE` when the last life is lost (gameover frame 1502).
> The hero's frame `$5B06` = `$7F` (the blank sprite), Room `$5C01` = `$28` and the room set-up `$9855`; the respawn state too: room `$28` (`$5C2D`), StatusTimer 0 (`$5C2C`), Status `$1D` (`$5C2B`); `JP $AE85` with A = `$1D`: Status = `$1D`, StatusTimer = 0. Status `$1D` is Frozen `$A90E`, which only holds; SpaceScene `$B0B6`, room `$28`'s script, plays the asteroid striking (gameover frames 1509-1961) and sets GameOver; EndGame `$906D` follows (frame 1962). After the last life the respawn (`$9090`, LifeLost still set) restores the same room and event.
> The time running out, on a clone (work/stage2/probe_points.py A: the RZX state at 44000 in room `$3B`, the countdown poked to 0 days 0 hours 2 minutes): the pass after 0/0/0 falls in here (days wrap to 255, the clock goes on counting: 255/23/59), Room `$28` 10 frames after the poke, status 29 from frame 20, GameOver `$5BFF` at frame 430: the same space scene as the last life's (no other end for the time running out).
> Witness: L1 1 (gameover).

@module util
$9390 c Random ; A pseudo-random byte from R and a 16-bit linear congruential state
> RandomState `$93AD` = RandomState * 257 + 41 (mod 65536: HL + L * 256 + `$29`); then with HL = `$8F47` + the state's low byte, A = (R XOR H) + L. `$8F47` is only an odd constant: nothing is read there (the SkoolKit "stride table" is not one). Out: A; HL and DE kept, flags changed.
> The only caller is `$BFA9` in `$BFA0` (382 calls over all builds).
> Witness: L1 382 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$93A2 ; the constant $8F47, not an address
$93AD w RandomState ; Random's 16-bit state: 12345 ($3039) as loaded
> Read and written only by Random `$9390`.

@module menu ; The title and device menu
$93AF c DeviceMenu ; The title and device menu: the frame, the logo, the options, the credits; keys 1-3 and 0
> Called by NewGame `$8F47` before every game (c1 2, explorers 5, gameover 1, rzx50000 1). Clears the screen, attributes `$44` (green ink), a 6 x 6 block of `$45` at `$5937` and a 3 x 3 block of `$47` at `$5942` (FillAttrs `$9526`).
> The frame is cut from the panel kept at `$E000-$E7FF` (the panel's screen third as loaded; after a game the one EndGame `$906D` saved): the panel's top row `$E000` to row 0, its bottom row `$E0E0` to row 23 (CopyCharRow `$94B0`), and the left and right edge cells of panel rows 1 and 2 (`$E020`, `$E040`) alternately down rows 1-22 (CopyEdgeCells `$94C2`, 11 times).
> The TERRAMEX logo TitleLogo `$95FD`, 3 rows of 25 cells at `$4063` (row 3, column 3), attribute `$46` (yellow); `$9F27` (the menu's pictures); the options MenuText `$9540` at row 8 column 8 (attribute `$44`) and the credits CreditsText `$9579` at row 17 column 2 (attribute `$47`) through PrintString `$94F9`.
> The loop (MenuLoop `$9440`), once a frame: the option box (rows 8-12, columns 8-21) gets attribute `$43` (magenta), the row of the chosen device (InputDevice `$94AF`: row 8 + 2 * device) `$47` (white); HALT; keys 1, 2, 3 (half row `$F7FE`) choose keyboard, Kempston, Sinclair (explorers: all three); key 0 (half row `$EFFE`) returns. IY = 0 at every turn is never used here.
> Witness: L1 9 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx).
$93C8 ; a 6 x 6 block of attribute $45 at row 9, column 23
$93D3 ; a 3 x 3 block of attribute $47 at row 10, column 2
$93DE ; the frame's top: the panel's top row
$93E7 ; the frame's bottom: the panel's bottom row
$93F0 ; the frame's sides: rows 1-22
$93F5 MenuFrameSides
$9403 ; the logo: 3 rows of 25 cells at row 3, column 3
$940B MenuLogoRow
$940F MenuLogoCell
$9413 MenuLogoByte
$941E ; attribute $46
$942D ; the menu's pictures
$9430 ; the options
$9433 ; the credits at row 17, column 2, attribute $47
$9440 c MenuLoop ; The device menu's loop: the option box and the chosen device's bar (DeviceMenu continued)
> Reached by falling in from DeviceMenu `$93AF` and from MenuKeys `$9468` (`JR $9440`) once a frame; an entry of the cut because the explorers recording starts inside the menu. The box (5 rows x 14 columns at row 8, column 8) gets attribute `$43`, the row of the chosen device (InputDevice `$94AF`; row 8 + 2 * device) `$47` on its 14 columns. IY = 0 here is never used. Falls into MenuKeys.
> Witness: L1 6835 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx).
$9440 ; the box: 5 rows x 14 columns of attribute $43 at row 8, column 8
$9450 ; the chosen device's row: 2 rows per option
$9464 ; 14 attributes of $47
$9468 c MenuKeys ; The device menu's keys: 1-3 choose the device, 0 starts (DeviceMenu continued)
> HALT (one turn a frame), then half row `$F7FE`: a lone 1, 2 or 3 sets InputDevice `$94AF` to 0 (keyboard), 1 (Kempston), 2 (Sinclair); half row `$EFFE` bit 0, the key 0, returns from DeviceMenu `$93AF` to NewGame; else `JR $9440`. explorers chooses all three devices; c1 1, 3, 2 then 0.
> Witness: L1 6836 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx).
$9468 ; one turn a frame
$9469 ; keys 1-5
$9474 ; 1: E = 0 (keyboard), 2: 1 (Kempston), 3: 2 (Sinclair)
$9484 MenuSetDevice
$9488 MenuCheckStart ; key 0 starts the game

@module interrupt ; The IM 2 handler and the AY music call
$9491 c Im2Handler ; The IM 2 handler: the AY music from RAM 6 on a 128K
> Reached through the vector `JP $9491` at `$5F5F` on every interrupt (83616 runs: one a frame in every build after GameEntry). On a 128K (Has128K `$5FFE` not 0) it pages RAM 6 in (`$7FFD` = `$16`), calls the music player at `$C000` and pages back the value in Last7FFD `$5FE5`; AF and BC are kept, the player keeps the rest. On a 48K it only enables the interrupts again: no music.
> Witness: L1 83616 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$9499 ; RAM 6, ROM 1
$94A0 ; the music player (part MUS)
$94A3 ; the page the game had
$94AC Im2Done

@module menu
$94AF b InputDevice ; The control device: 0 keyboard, 1 Kempston, 2 Sinclair
> Set by DeviceMenu `$93AF` (keys 1, 2, 3; c1 and explorers), read by the input routine `$B894` in play.
$94B0 c CopyCharRow ; Copy a character row of 32 cells (8 pixel rows)
> HL = the source, DE = the destination, both at a cell's top pixel row in a screen-like layout. 32 bytes a pixel row, INC H and INC D between rows. Callers: DeviceMenu `$93E4`, `$93ED`.
> Witness: L1 18 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx).
$94B2 CopyCharRowLoop
$94C2 c CopyEdgeCells ; Copy the left and right edge cells of a row; DE to the next character row
> HL = the source row (the left cell), DE = the destination row. Copies the cell at column 0, then the cell at column 31 of both (L OR `$1F`, E OR `$1F`), through CopyCell `$94E4`. Out: DE = the next character row's column 0 (into the next screen third after row 7 of one); HL unchanged. Called 22 times a menu by DeviceMenu.
> Witness: L1 198 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx).
$94DF ; past the third's last row: the next third
$94E4 c CopyCell ; Copy one cell, 8 pixel rows
> HL = the source, DE = the destination; INC H and INC D between rows. BC kept. Called by CopyEdgeCells `$94C2`.
> Witness: L1 396 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx).
$94E7 CopyCellLoop
$94EF c PrintMenuText ; Print the device options at row 8, column 8, attribute $44
> DE = MenuText `$9540`, HL = `$4808`, A' = `$44`; falls into PrintString `$94F9`. Called by DeviceMenu `$9430`.
> Witness: L1 9 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx).
$94F9 c PrintString ; Print a text with an attribute: 0 ends, $0D a new line
> DE = the text, HL = the screen address of the first cell, A' = the attribute. Each character goes through PrintChar `$90C6` and its cell's attribute (ScreenToAttr `$9536`) is A'. `$0D` starts the next character row under the line's first cell: the line start is kept in the operand at `$9517` (written here, so the image after a menu holds `$50A2`, the credits' last line); 0 ends. `$7F` is the ROM font's copyright sign.
> Callers: PrintMenuText `$94EF` (falls in), DeviceMenu `$943D`, and `$A7EB` (the countdown text, not executed in any recording).
> Witness: L1 108 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx).
$94F9 ; the line start: the operand at $9517
$94FC PrintStringLoop
$950E ; the cell's attribute = A'
$9516 PrintNewLine ; LD HL,n: n = the line start, written at $94F9
$9519 ; the next character row, the next third after row 7 of one
$9525 b UnusedRet ; A lone RET ($C9) that no code reaches
> No jump, call or table in the image names `$9525`; never executed or read in any recording.
$9526 c FillAttrs ; Fill a block of B rows by C bytes with A, rows 32 bytes apart
> HL = the top-left address (an attribute in every caller), B = the rows, C = the bytes a row, A = the value. Out: HL = the address below the block; BC changed. Callers: DeviceMenu `$93D0`, `$93DB` and MenuLoop `$944D` (once a frame on the menu).
> Witness: L1 34256 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx).
$9528 FillAttrsRow
$9536 c ScreenToAttr ; The attribute address of a cell's screen address
> HL = a screen address at a cell's top row. Out: H = `$58` + the screen third, L unchanged: the cell's attribute. Callers: DeviceMenu `$941B`, PrintString `$950B`.
> Witness: L1 2268 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx).
$9540 t MenuText ; The device options: four lines a blank line apart, 0 ends
> Printed by PrintMenuText `$94EF` at row 8, column 8: "1 : KEYBOARD", "2 : KEMPSTON", "3 : SINCLAIR", "0 : START GAME", with `$0D $0D` between them (rows 8, 10, 12, 14). The option box of MenuLoop `$9440` covers rows 8-12.
$954E ; 2 : KEMPSTON
$955C ; 3 : SINCLAIR
$956A ; 0 : START GAME, then 0
