@module player ; The hero: tile probes, walking, climbing, falling, the room exits, the controls
$A0FE b HeroProbes 4 ; The hero's four contact flags, cleared and set by $A102 each time it runs
> $A102 (IY = $A0FE) zeroes them and its tile tests set them. Of their uses: +0 and +1 are tested by $A34B before it turns the velocity $5C34 round (+0 when moving left, +1 when moving right), +3 is tested by $AD17 after a climb step and in $A34B for downward moves (known only from the code; the meanings are GC's). 83 554 reads and 150 559 writes over the builds.
$A102 c HeroTileChecks ; Probe the tiles around the hero: deadly tile, floor distance, mud, walls (SK, renamed)
> IX = the hero ($5B04). Clears the probe record $A0FE (IY) and fills it: +3 the rows down to a floor (FloorDistance $A1F4), +0 / +1 a wall at the left / right edge (LeftWallCheck $A2AC, RightWallCheck $A2FA). While the status $5C06 is 0 and the normal tile set is in ($918C = 0) it first reads the two tiles under the feet (DeadlyTileProbe $A176): tile $A5 under either sets status $1A (the fall death, FallDeath $A888). Standing (+3 = 0) on tile $BC or $BD with the normal set stores the tile in $5C28 and counts passes in $5C29; at 50 passes status $11 (SinkInMud $AA04). Off it, $5C29 = 0. When $5BA0 is 0 (the hero stands on the lift, LiftPlatform $AF81) +3 is forced to 0.
> Out: $A0FE filled, IY = $A0FE; DE kept. Called from HeroUpdate $A3E1 ($A50E, $A576), FloatInRoom2C $A34B, BalloonRide $AC35, BalloonCrash $AC1A, BounceUp $AD17, JumpArc $ADAC and JumpStepY $AE37.
> Evidence: the $A5 test never matched in any recording ($A126 / $A12B: 11772 tests, no match); $BC / $BD matched 26 passes in one rzx segment, the 50-pass sink never came ($A15A not executed).
> Witness: L1 21714 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$A114 ; the probes for deadly tiles only when the status is 0 ...
$A11A ; ... and the normal tile set is in
$A12D DeadlyTileHit ; tile $A5 under the feet: status $1A, the fall death
$A132 ProbeFloor ; +3 = rows down to a floor tile
$A145 ; HL points at the matched entry of the floor list: the floor tile itself
$A14E OnMudTile ; $5C28 = the tile ($BC or $BD), $5C29 counts the passes on it
$A156 ; 50 passes on mud: status $11 (sink)
$A161 OffMudTile ; not on mud: the count restarts
$A165 ProbeWalls ; +0 left edge, +1 right edge
$A16B ; on the lift ($5BA0 = 0) the hero always stands
$A174 HeroTileChecksEnd
$A176 c DeadlyTileProbe ; Read the two tiles under the hero's feet
