> The room script of room $3C. RoomStage $5C41 counts the passes in the room to $14; at $14, if PillsTaken $5C3F is 0 (the pills, item $16, never picked up: PickUpItem $BB96 sets it), stage $15 and status $17 (SilentDeath $A8A8); with the pills it stays at $14. Witness: rzx26000 runs it 214 times, PillsTaken set (rzx14500 picks the pills up, $BB96 once); the death branch ($B796) is not executed in any recording (c1, explorers, gameover, the 31 rzx builds).
> Witness: L1 214 (rzx).
$B791 RadiationCheck ; 20 passes in the room: the pills?
$B796 ; no pills: status $17
$B79C c FloorRoom36 ; Room $36: the flickering hazard floor, 21 tiles of row 10 from column 0
> B = 21 tiles from the tile map's $F940 (row 10), then FlickerFloor $B7A8. Witness: rzx20000 runs it 155 times.
> Witness: L1 155 (rzx).
$B7A3 c FloorRoom35 ; Room $35: the flickering hazard floor, 11 tiles of row 10 from column 20
> B = 11 tiles from $F954, then FlickerFloor $B7A8. Witness: rzx20000 runs it 187 times.
> Witness: L1 187 (rzx).
$B7A8 c FlickerFloor ; Write the hazard tiles $BC / $BD along the floor, alternating, and keep slot $5B14 on the explorer
> B = the tile count, HL = the first tile map byte. For each tile (the loop runs the whole body again): Y of the creature slots $5B09, $5B0D, $5B11 = 0, slot $5B14 at the explorer's X and 8 pixels below him (not below Y $5A), then the tile $BC + (B & 1) XOR (PassCount / 2 & 1) written through $9A4D. So the floor alternates $BC / $BD tile by tile and swaps every second pass; $BC and $BD are the tiles $A102 counts when stood on (SK: 50 of them set status $11, SinkInMud $AA04; GC's range). What slot $5B14 shows here is known only from the code (a run request).
> Witness: L1 5312 (rzx).
$B7C4 FlickerTile ; the tile: $BC or $BD by tile parity and PassCount bit 1
$B7DD c RunRoomScript ; Run the script of the room: the word of RoomScripts $B7EC
> HL = RoomScripts + 2 x Room ($5C01), then $A6DD jumps to the word (none when 0), with DE kept. Called every pass by $A3E1 with IX = the explorer object $5B04.
> Witness: L1 26517 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$B7EC w RoomScripts 12 ; The per-room script of each room $00-$47: a routine address, 0 for none
> RunRoomScript $B7DD jumps to word Room ($5C01) through $A6DD every pass, with IX = the explorer object $5B04; a zero word does nothing. 72 words: the 70 map rooms $00-$45 and the two rooms $46, $47 that only the portals reach. 21 rooms have a script; the ones in this range: $17 and $1A the snakes ($B55A, $B562), $2D the cricket ball ($B370), $35 and $36 the flickering floor ($B7A3, $B79C), $39 the Silver Cross ($B4E2), $3B the professor ($B5DD), $3C the radiation ($B784), $3E and $40 the lever ($B72D, $B723), $3F the basket ($B409), $43 the Silver Lining ($B704). The others go to $AFD7 (rooms $03, $0F), $B16A ($12), $B0B6 ($28), $A34B ($2C), $B263 ($2E), $B22D ($2F), $B2EB ($46) and $B18A ($47).
> Witness: the play builds read the words of the rooms they visit (rzx16000 and rzx18000 read word $2D, rzx42000-rzx50000 word $3B); words $46 and $47 are read only by the load in c1.
$B7EC ; level 0, rooms $00-$0B: $03 $AFD7
$B804 ; level 1, rooms $0C-$17: $0F $AFD7, $12 $B16A, $17 $B55A
$B81C ; level 2, rooms $18-$23: $1A $B562
$B834 ; level 3, rooms $24-$2F: $28 $B0B6, $2C $A34B, $2D $B370, $2E $B263, $2F $B22D
$B84C ; level 4, rooms $30-$3B: $35 $B7A3, $36 $B79C, $39 $B4E2, $3B $B5DD
$B864 ; level 5, rooms $3C-$47: $3C $B784, $3E $B72D, $3F $B409, $40 $B723, $43 $B704, $46 $B2EB, $47 $B18A

@module player
$B87C b InputBits ; The controls read this pass: bit 0 right, 1 left, 2 down, 3 up, 4 fire
> Written by ReadDevice $B894 every call (cleared, then the bits of the pressed controls) and read back at its end ($B930). Witness: written in all 34 builds (52351 writes).
$B87D c ReadControls ; Read the controls; both left and right, or both up and down, read as nothing
> Out: A = the InputBits of ReadDevice $B894, or 0 when bits 0 and 1 or bits 2 and 3 are both set; E = the raw InputBits on every path. Called by $A3E1 every pass ($A3F4), by $A34B ($A356), by $AF81 ($AFBA, which tests E: up + down there gives down, status 20) and by TelescopeRoom $B16A ($B17F).
> Witness: L1 26612 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx). The cancel branches ($B887, $B890) are not executed in any recording (c1, explorers, gameover, the 31 rzx builds).
$B889 ReadControlsUpDown ; up and down both?
$B892 ReadControlsDone
$B894 c ReadDevice ; Read the chosen device into InputBits: keyboard, Kempston or Sinclair
> Device $94AF (the device menu: 0 keyboard, 1 Kempston, 2 Sinclair). Keyboard (ReadKeyboard $B8FE): SPACE fire, Z left, X right, O up, K down (the Help page of the selector: "Z=Left X=Right O=Up K=Down <SPACE> -Jump"). Kempston: IN ($1F) AND $1F, already in the InputBits order. Sinclair (port $EFFE, keys 6-0): 0 fire, 6 left, 7 right, 9 up, 8 down. Out: A = InputBits $B87C.
> Witness: explorers reads all three (keyboard 849 and Sinclair 853 passes, Kempston in every build).
> Witness: L1 26612 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$B8A3 ; device 2: Sinclair, keys 6 7 8 9 0
$B8B0 SinclairLeft ; 6: left
$B8B6 SinclairRight ; 7: right
$B8BC SinclairUp ; 9: up
$B8C2 SinclairDown ; 8: down
$B8CC ReadKempston ; device 1: Kempston port $1F
$B8D4 c ReadCursorKeys ; A Cursor joystick reader no device reaches: 5 left, 8 right, 7 up, 6 down, 0 fire
> The same form as the other readers (HL = InputBits): port $F7FE bit 4 (5) left; port $EFFE bit 0 (0) fire, bit 2 (8) right, bit 3 (7) up, bit 4 (6) down; then JP $B930, but a released 6 returns at once (RET NZ at $B8F8) with A = the port byte instead of InputBits. ReadDevice $B894 sends every device but 0 and 1 to the Sinclair reader, and no instruction of the image refers to $B8D4: a fourth device left out of the menu. Not executed in any recording (c1, explorers, gameover, the 31 rzx builds); known only from the code.
> Witness: L1 0 ().
$B8D9 ; 5 (port $F7FE bit 4): left
$B8DF CursorRow2 ; port $EFFE: 0 fire
$B8EA CursorRight ; 8: right
$B8F0 CursorUp ; 7: up
$B8F6 CursorDown ; 6: down; RET NZ when released (A = the port byte)
$B8FE c ReadKeyboard ; The keyboard: SPACE fire, Z left, X right, O up, K down
> Reached from ReadDevice $B894 when Device $94AF is 0. Witness: explorers, 849 passes.
> Witness: L1 849 (explorers).
$B909 KeyZ ; Z (port $FEFE bit 1): left
$B914 KeyX ; X (bit 2): right
$B91A KeyO ; O (port $DFFE bit 1): up
$B925 KeyK ; K (port $BFFE bit 2): down
$B930 c InputBitsOut ; A = InputBits: the end of every reader
> Witness: L1 26612 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).

@module objects ; The items: where they lie, pick up, the bearers, the swap
$B932 c ResetItems ; Put every item back: clear the taken bit of all 31 ItemPlaces records
> Called by InitGame at $8F83 (a new game); InitGame then marks the Energy Crystal of room $30 taken ($8F86). Witness: c1 once, explorers 5 times, rzx00000 once (the new games).
> Witness: L1 7 (c1, explorers, rzx).
$B937 ResetItemsLoop
$B93F c SpawnRoomItems ; Fill the two item slots with the items of this room
> Both item slots $5C0E and $5C13 emptied (item $FF: IX+2 and IX+7), then the 31 ItemPlaces $B99D records are scanned for Room ($5C01) and each match goes to PlaceItem $B95F, C counting the matches. Taken items carry bit 7 in their room byte and never match. Called on every room entry ($9911, the end of the room set-up), after a gift to the professor ($B5F8) and after the crystal is placed ($BA27).
> Witness: L1 113 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx).
$B955 SpawnRoomItemsLoop
$B95F c PlaceItem ; Put the item of an ItemPlaces record into the next free item slot
> HL = the record, C = the slots used so far (0, 1; 2 and more: the record is ignored). The slot ($5C0E for C = 0, $5C13 for C = 1) gets X, Y and the item (byte 1 & $1F) decoded from the record (ItemPlaces $B99D) and the record's address in its bytes +3 and +4, for PickUpItem $BB6C to mark it taken. Out: C + 1; HL, AF, B kept.
> Witness: L1 42 (c1, explorers, gameover, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx, rzx). The second slot ($B96A) is used 3 times (gameover, rzx10000, rzx14500).
$B96E PlaceItemSlot ; the record's address into slot +3, +4
$B983 ; X = (byte2 & 3) x 64 + (byte1 & $E0) / 4
$B992 ; Y = (byte2 & $FC) x 2
$B99D b ItemPlaces 3 ; Where the items lie: 31 records of 3 bytes, [room + taken bit, item, position]
> Byte 0: the room ($00-$47) in bits 0-6, bit 7 set when the item has been taken (PickUpItem $BB6C sets it through the record address the slot keeps; it then matches no room). Byte 1: the item (0-31, an index into the item sprites $8400) in bits 0-4 and bits 3-5 of X in bits 5-7. Byte 2: bits 6-7 of X in bits 0-1 and Y / 8 in bits 2-7 (byte2 & $FC = Y / 2). So X = (byte2 & 3) * 64 + (byte1 & $E0) / 4 and Y = (byte2 & $FC) * 2, both multiples of 8 (PlaceItem $B95F). Checked live: record 15 (room $21, Barrel Small, byte2 $24) lies at X $28, Y $48 (work/stage2/probe_points.py).
> ResetItems $B932 clears every taken bit at a new game; InitGame then sets the one of record 20 ($B9D9, the Energy Crystal of room $30) at $8F86, so that crystal is not there until the explorer puts it in place (ItemsPass $B9FA clears the bit again). SpawnRoomItems $B93F scans the records for the room on every room entry and puts the first two matches in the item slots $5C0E and $5C13; no room has more than two. The Formula (15) lies in each of the four portal rooms $2E, $2F, $46, $47; rooms $10 and $1D hold two items each.
> The item names are those of the SkoolKit notes (SK, Items-Format.md); in-play checks: the pickups the play builds make (PickUpItem $BBE4, 22 runs in 13 builds).
$B99D ; 0: room $00, item 5 Umbrella, X $A0, Y $08
$B9A0 ; 1: room $07, item 9 Barrel Medium, X $80, Y $40
$B9A3 ; 2: room $08, item 11 ACME Expanding Bridge, X $A0, Y $08
